 "root_cause": "The level bias is dominated by the P(active) factor: the incumbent multiplied P(stat>=k | involved) by a raw appearance rate (~0.82-0.89) computed over every player who appeared, while the players the exchange lists are involved ~97-100% of the time (listing is itself selection information). A market-free involvement model trained on earlier seasons is far better calibrated on the at-risk universe (log loss 0.41 vs 0.60) but cannot reproduce the listing selection (P_inv ~0.86 on listed players). Threshold semantics are correct (settlement = stat >= threshold) and the conditional mean is not biased low. A secondary, validated effect is the pooled negative-binomial shape for yardage."
